    "created_at": "2018-02-16T16:38:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-16T16:38:17Z",
    "body": "I think it's still useful to use MIME types as the canonical label for given parsers, even if they're not exposed to web developers.\r\n\r\nWe _could_ call this spec the \"resource sniffer algorithm\" and make up our own ad-hoc labels for each format/parser, but that doesn't seem like a useful thing to do when MIME types already exist.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
